G2228.def:
ἤ, 
disjunctive and comparative particle (Bl., §36, 12; 77, 11); 
__1. disjunctive, or; 
__(a) between single words: Matthieu 5:17 Marc 6:56, Luc 2:24, Jean 6:19, Romains 1:21, al.; 
__(b) before a sentence expressing a variation, denial or refutation of a previous statement, frequently in interrog. form: Matthieu 7:4, 9 Marc 12:14, Luc 13:4, Romains 3:29 6:3 9:21, 1 Corinthiens 6:9, 16 9:6, 2 Corinthiens 11:7; ἤ . . . ἤ, either . . . or, Matthieu 6:24, Luc 16:13, 1 Corinthiens 14:6; 
__(with) in a disjunctive question (as Lat. an after utrum): Matthieu 9:5, Marc 2:9, Luc 7:19, al.; after πότερον, Jean 7:17; μή, 1 Corinthiens 9:8; μήτι, 2 Corinthiens 1:17; ἤ . . . ἤ . . . ἤ, Marc 13:35. 
__2. Comparative, than: after comparatives, Matthieu 10:15, Luc 9:13, Jean 3:19, Romains 13:11, al.; after ἕτερον, Actes 17:21; θέλω (Khüner 3, iv, 303), 1 Corinthiens 14:19; πρὶν ἤ, before, before accusative and inf., Matthieu 1:18 Marc 14:30; after a positive adj. (Genèse 49:12; cf. Robertson, Gr., 661), Matthieu 18:8, 9 Marc 9:43, 45 47. 
__3. with other particles: ἀλλ᾽ ἤ, see: ἀλλά; ἤ γάρ, see: γάρ; ἢ καί, or even, or also, Matthieu 7:10, Luc 11:11, 12 Romains 2:15 4:9, al; ἤτοι . . . ἤ, Romains 6:16 (cf. Wis.11:19).

G2244.def:
ἡλικία, -ας, ἡ
(ἧλιξ, of the same age, mature), [in LXX: Eze.13:18 (קוֹמָה), Job 29:18, Wis.4:9, Sir.26:17, frequently in 2-4 Mac ;] 
always of age or maturity; "a stage of growth whether measured by age or stature"; 
__1. (a) age: Matthieu 6:27, Luc 12:25 (R, mg.), Hébreux 11:11; 
__(b) full age, maturity: Jean 9:21, 23, Éphésiens 4:13. 
__2. stature: Luc 19:3 (Matthieu 6:27, Luc 12:25, AV, R, txt.; but the prevailing usage in LXX and π. favours the former meaning in these doubtful passages; cf., Ellic., ICC, AR, on Eph, l.with; Milligan, NTD, 74 f., and esp., MM, Exp., xv; e contra, Field, Notes, 6).†

